.SH NAME
messq-auth-check - verify a credential from stdin against an auth-file


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmessq auth check [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Check whether a credential matches SOME entry of the named auth-file and
exit 0 on match, 1 on mismatch — the yes/no shape deployment jobs want
before they ship a rotated secret. The credential arrives on stdin whole,
one trailing LF/CRLF stripped exactly like \fBmessq auth hash\fR\&. A mismatch
always names the usual suspects, including the DLQ nuance: an exact grant
like 'orders' never covers 'orders.dlq', while a trailing 'orders*' does.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--auth-file\fP=""
	token file to verify against (or MESSQ_AUTH_FILE)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for check


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--addr\fP="unix:///run/messq/messq.sock"
	daemon address (unix://, http://, https://)

.PP
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	colour: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--full-ids\fP[=false]
	print full ULIDs instead of abbreviated ones

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="auto"
	output mode: auto|table|json|ndjson

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress narration; data and errors unaffected

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	per-request deadline (0 = none)

.PP
\fB--token-file\fP=""
	file holding the bearer token, mode 0600

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	narrate (-vv dumps each HTTP exchange and the resolved config)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  printf '%s' "$NEW_CRED" | messq auth check --auth-file /etc/messq/tokens && echo rotate-ok # noexec: shell pipeline carrying a credential
.EE


